{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/color"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric"]]},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"color","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLyricV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric\/color"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLyric":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLyric"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLyric"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric","role":"symbol","title":"MXLLyric","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lyric type represents text underlays for lyrics. Two text elements that are not separated by an elision"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element are part of the same syllable, but may have different text formatting. The MusicXML XSD is more strict"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than the DTD in enforcing this by disallowing a second syllabic element unless preceded by an elision element."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The lyric number indicates multiple lines, though a name can be used as well. Common name examples are verse"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and chorus."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLyric/color":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric\